<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>More Preliminary</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Fundamentals of Diffusion Large Language Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Masking Process.</span>
Given a clean sample <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, diffusion large language models (dLLM) forward process progressively replaces tokens with a special token <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span> as a function of time <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. At time <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the data point <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is fully observed with no masks, while at <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, all tokens are guaranteed to be masked. For a given <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the sequence <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is partially masked: each token <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is masked with probability <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and remains with probability <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-t</annotation></semantics></math>. The transition probability for the noised sequence <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t|0}(x_{t}\mid x_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{N}q_{t|0}(x_{t}^{i}\mid x_{0}^{i}),\quad\text{where}\;q_{t|0}(x_{t}^{i}\mid x_{0}^{i})=\begin{cases}1-t,&amp;x_{t}^{i}=x_{0}^{i},\\
t,&amp;x_{t}^{i}=\texttt{[MASK]}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">[MASK]</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t|0}(x_{t}\mid x_{0})=\prod_{i=1}^{N}q_{t|0}(x_{t}^{i}\mid x_{0}^{i}),\quad\text{where}\;q_{t|0}(x_{t}^{i}\mid x_{0}^{i})=\begin{cases}1-t,&amp;x_{t}^{i}=x_{0}^{i},\\
t,&amp;x_{t}^{i}=\texttt{[MASK]}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">M</span> denotes the special mask token <span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reverse Unmasking Process.</span>
The forward process is reversible: the corresponding reverse process iteratively unmasks tokens, progressively evolving from <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> back to <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al., 2021b</a>)</cite>. Specifically, while masked positions either retain their masked state with some probability or undergo decoding to concrete tokens based on the model’s predictive distribution.
However, directly reversing Eq. <a href="#A1.Ex1" title="A.1 Fundamentals of Diffusion Large Language Models ‣ Appendix A More Preliminary ‣ Accelerating Diffusion LLM Inference via Local Determinism Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> is inefficient in practice, since it generally unmasks just one token per. A common remedy is the <em id="A1.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-leaping</em> approximation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gillespie, 2001</a>)</cite>, which allows transitions from time <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to an earlier <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq s&lt;t\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq s&lt;t\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>) that simultaneously unmask multiple tokens.</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{s|t}=\prod_{i=1}^{N}q_{s|t}(x_{s}^{i}\mid x_{t}),\quad\text{where}\;q_{s|t}(x_{s}^{i}\mid x_{t})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;x_{t}^{i}\neq\texttt{M},\;x_{s}^{i}=x_{t}^{i},\\
\frac{s}{t},&amp;x_{t}^{i}=\texttt{M},\;x_{s}^{i}=\texttt{M},\\
\frac{t-s}{t}\,q_{0|t}(x_{s}^{i}\mid x_{t}),&amp;x_{t}^{i}=\texttt{M},\;x_{s}^{i}\neq\texttt{M},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">M</mtext><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">M</mtext><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">M</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">M</mtext><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">M</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{s|t}=\prod_{i=1}^{N}q_{s|t}(x_{s}^{i}\mid x_{t}),\quad\text{where}\;q_{s|t}(x_{s}^{i}\mid x_{t})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;x_{t}^{i}\neq\texttt{M},\;x_{s}^{i}=x_{t}^{i},\\
\frac{s}{t},&amp;x_{t}^{i}=\texttt{M},\;x_{s}^{i}=\texttt{M},\\
\frac{t-s}{t}\,q_{0|t}(x_{s}^{i}\mid x_{t}),&amp;x_{t}^{i}=\texttt{M},\;x_{s}^{i}\neq\texttt{M},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{0|t}(\cdot\mid x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0|t}(\cdot\mid x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is a categorical distribution over vocabulary <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> that predicts a non-<span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span> token at a masked position given the visible context <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We establish theoretical guarantees for our LocalLeap parallel decoding scheme.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Definition</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{i_{1},\dots,i_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of masked positions to be decoded.
For each <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for some small <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{*}=p_{j}(X_{i_{j}}=x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})&gt;1-\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{*}=p_{j}(X_{i_{j}}=x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})&gt;1-\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">be the model-assigned probability of the candidate token <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i_{j}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i_{j}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> under context <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We partition <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> into disjoint clusters
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{C}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{C}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each cluster <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> contains exactly one <em id="A2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">anchor</em> position <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with high confidence <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{a}^{*}\geq\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{a}^{*}\geq\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, and its local neighborhood <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}=\{j\in\mathcal{D}\mid|j-a|\leq W\wedge j\neq a\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}=\{j\in\mathcal{D}\mid|j-a|\leq W\wedge j\neq a\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{*}\geq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{*}\geq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the number of neighbors in <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=|\mathcal{N}|\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=|\mathcal{N}|\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume thresholds satisfy <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2&lt;\tau&lt;\kappa&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2&lt;\tau&lt;\kappa&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Define per-token error parameters</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{a}&lt;1-\kappa,\quad\epsilon_{n}&lt;1-\tau,\quad\epsilon_{\max}=\max(\epsilon_{a},\epsilon_{n})&lt;1-\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{a}&lt;1-\kappa,\quad\epsilon_{n}&lt;1-\tau,\quad\epsilon_{\max}=\max(\epsilon_{a},\epsilon_{n})&lt;1-\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the aggregate error budget in the cluster</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(X_{i_{j}}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})=\epsilon_{a}+m\epsilon_{n}&lt;(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(X_{i_{j}}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})=\epsilon_{a}+m\epsilon_{n}&lt;(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Equivalence for Sequential Decoding</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> is the maximizer uniquely of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Define the product-of-marginals probability mass function (PMF):</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=\prod_{j=1}^{n}p_{j}(X_{i_{j}}=z_{j}\mid\mathcal{E})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=\prod_{j=1}^{n}p_{j}(X_{i_{j}}=z_{j}\mid\mathcal{E}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Maximizing <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> factorizes into maximizing each marginal <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}(X_{i_{j}}=z_{j}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}(X_{i_{j}}=z_{j}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> independently. Since <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{*}\geq\tau&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{*}\geq\tau&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, each <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i_{j}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i_{j}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique maximizer of its marginal distribution. Hence,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmax_{\bm{z}}q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=(x_{i_{1}}^{*},\dots,x_{i_{n}}^{*})=\bm{x}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmax_{\bm{z}}q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=(x_{i_{1}}^{*},\dots,x_{i_{n}}^{*})=\bm{x}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Condition for <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to maximize <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> For a cluster <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+m</annotation></semantics></math> elements, the joint probability of the configuration <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> can be lower bounded by Bonferroni’s inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=p\Big(\bigcap_{j\in\mathcal{C}}\{X_{i_{j}}=x_{i_{j}}^{*}\}\Big|\mathcal{E}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p\Big(\bigcap_{j\in\mathcal{C}}\{X_{i_{j}}=x_{i_{j}}^{*}\}\Big|\mathcal{E}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(X_{i_{j}}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(X_{i_{j}}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;1-\big((1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;1-\big((1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For any alternative sequence <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{n})\neq\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}=(y_{1},\ldots,y_{n})\neq\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists at least one coordinate <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. For such <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(X_{i_{j}}=y_{j}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq p(X_{i_{j}}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq\epsilon_{\max}=1-\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(X_{i_{j}}=y_{j}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq p(X_{i_{j}}\neq x_{i_{j}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq\epsilon_{\max}=1-\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{y}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq 1-\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq 1-\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">To guarantee <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly more probable than any alternative, it suffices that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\big((1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)\big)&gt;1-\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\big((1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)\big)&gt;1-\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">which simplifies to the cluster-level certification condition:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)&lt;\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)&lt;\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When each cluster <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the above inequality, <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique maximizer of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since clusters are disjoint, the global maximizer under <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the concatenation of all cluster-level maximizers:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmax_{\bm{z}}p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=\argmax_{\bm{z}}q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=\bm{x}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>𝐳</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmax_{\bm{z}}p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=\argmax_{\bm{z}}q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})=\bm{x}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Neighbor Capacity Bound.</span> For a cluster <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> containing one anchor and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> neighbors, the certification condition</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)&lt;\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">is equivalent to an explicit upper bound on the number of neighbors:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&lt;\frac{\tau-(1-\kappa)}{1-\tau}=\frac{\kappa}{1-\tau}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&lt;\frac{\tau-(1-\kappa)}{1-\tau}=\frac{\kappa}{1-\tau}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, the maximal admissible number of neighbors per anchor is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\max}=\left\lfloor\frac{\kappa}{1-\tau}-1\right\rfloor." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\max}=\left\lfloor\frac{\kappa}{1-\tau}-1\right\rfloor.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">This bound guarantees that parallel commitments within each cluster are consistent with the sequential greedy decoding.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span><math id="A2.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> distance is bounded</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For discrete distributions <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> distance as:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p-q\|_{p}^{p}=|p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}+\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p-q\|_{p}^{p}=|p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}+\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{j}=\{X_{i_{j}}=x_{i_{j}}^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}=\{X_{i_{j}}=x_{i_{j}}^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{*}=p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})=p\Big(\bigcap_{j\in\mathcal{C}}A_{j}\}\Big),\quad q^{*}=q(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}=p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})=p\Big(\bigcap_{j\in\mathcal{C}}A_{j}\}\Big),\quad q^{*}=q(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounds for <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> We first establish upper and lower bounds for <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Boole’s inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{*}=p\Big(\bigcap_{j\in\mathcal{C}}A_{j}\}\Big)=1-p\Big(\bigcup_{j\in\mathcal{C}}A_{j}^{c}\Big)\geq 1-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j}^{c})\geq 1-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}\epsilon_{j}=1-S." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}=p\Big(\bigcap_{j\in\mathcal{C}}A_{j}\}\Big)=1-p\Big(\bigcup_{j\in\mathcal{C}}A_{j}^{c}\Big)\geq 1-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j}^{c})\geq 1-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}\epsilon_{j}=1-S.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\epsilon_{a}+m\epsilon_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\epsilon_{a}+m\epsilon_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the aggregate error budget from the previous section.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the upper bound, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}=P\Big(\bigcap_{j}A_{j}\Big)\leq\min_{j\in\mathcal{C}}P(A_{j})=1-\epsilon_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}=P\Big(\bigcap_{j}A_{j}\Big)\leq\min_{j\in\mathcal{C}}P(A_{j})=1-\epsilon_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-S\leq p^{*}\leq 1-\epsilon_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-S\leq p^{*}\leq 1-\epsilon_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounds for <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> For the product-of-marginals distribution, by Weierstrass’s product inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j})=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}(1-\epsilon_{j})\geq 1-\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{j}=1-S." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j})=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}(1-\epsilon_{j})\geq 1-\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{j}=1-S.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">The upper bound follows directly:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j})=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}(1-\epsilon_{j})\leq\min_{j}(1-\epsilon_{j})=1-\epsilon_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}p(A_{j})=\prod_{j\in\mathcal{C}}(1-\epsilon_{j})\leq\min_{j}(1-\epsilon_{j})=1-\epsilon_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-S\leq q^{*}\leq 1-\epsilon_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-S\leq q^{*}\leq 1-\epsilon_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounding <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p^{*}-q^{*}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p^{*}-q^{*}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Since both <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> lie in the interval <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1-S,1-\epsilon_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1-S,1-\epsilon_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|p^{*}-q^{*}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|p^{*}-q^{*}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-\epsilon_{\max})-(1-\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{j})=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{j}-\epsilon_{\max}=S-\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-\epsilon_{\max})-(1-\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{j})=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\epsilon_{j}-\epsilon_{\max}=S-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1-\kappa)+(m-1)(1-\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1-\kappa)+(m-1)(1-\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounds for alternative sequences.</span> For any <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq\epsilon_{\max},\quad q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq\epsilon_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq\epsilon_{\max},\quad q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq\epsilon_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.8" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|\leq\epsilon_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" lspace="0.278em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|\leq\epsilon_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.9" class="ltx_p">On the other side,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}\big(p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})+q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})\big)=(1-p^{*})+(1-q^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}\big(p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})+q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})\big)=(1-p^{*})+(1-q^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\big(1-(1-S)\big)+\big(1-(1-S)\big)=2S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\big(1-(1-S)\big)+\big(1-(1-S)\big)=2S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.10" class="ltx_p">Using the supremum bound: for any sequence <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{i}|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{i}|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a_{i}|^{p}\leq M^{p-1}|a_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a_{i}|^{p}\leq M^{p-1}|a_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>. So,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\big(\sup_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|\big)^{p-1}\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\big(\sup_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|\big)^{p-1}\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\epsilon_{\max}^{p-1}\cdot 2S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\epsilon_{\max}^{p-1}\cdot 2S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> distance bound.</span> Combining the above results:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|p-q\|_{p}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|p-q\|_{p}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}+\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|p(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{x}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}+\sum_{\bm{z}\neq\bm{x}^{*}}|p(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})-q(\bm{z}\mid\mathcal{E})|^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(S-\epsilon_{\max})^{p}+(\epsilon_{\max}^{p-1}\cdot 2S)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(S-\epsilon_{\max})^{p}+(\epsilon_{\max}^{p-1}\cdot 2S)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total variation distance.</span> For the special case <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance is:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|p-q\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|p-q\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(S-\epsilon_{\max})+2S=3S-\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(S-\epsilon_{\max})+2S=3S-\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;3(1-\kappa)+(3m-1)(1-\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;3(1-\kappa)+(3m-1)(1-\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the total variation distance is bounded by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TV}(p,q)=\frac{1}{2}\|p-q\|_{1}&lt;\frac{1}{2}\big(3(1-\kappa)+(3m-1)(1-\tau)\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>TV</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TV}(p,q)=\frac{1}{2}\|p-q\|_{1}&lt;\frac{1}{2}\big(3(1-\kappa)+(3m-1)(1-\tau)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>KL divergence is bounded</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The total correlation between the joint distribution <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and the product-of-marginals <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the KL divergence, which can be expressed as the difference between the sum of marginal entropies and the joint entropy:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{TC}(p,q)=D_{KL}(p\|q)=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}H(X_{i_{j}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H(\bm{X}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>TC</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TC}(p,q)=D_{KL}(p\|q)=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{C}}H(X_{i_{j}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H(\bm{X}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the entropy chain rule:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{X}\mid\mathcal{E})=\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}H\big(X_{i_{k}}\mid X_{i_{1}},\dots,X_{i_{k-1}},\mathcal{E}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{X}\mid\mathcal{E})=\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}H\big(X_{i_{k}}\mid X_{i_{1}},\dots,X_{i_{k-1}},\mathcal{E}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting the chain rule decomposition:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex43.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">TC</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H(\bm{X}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H(\bm{X}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}\Big[H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H\big(X_{i_{k}}\mid X_{i_{1}},\dots,X_{i_{k-1}},\mathcal{E}\big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{m+1}\Big[H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H\big(X_{i_{k}}\mid X_{i_{1}},\dots,X_{i_{k-1}},\mathcal{E}\big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=2}^{m+1}I\big(X_{i_{k}};X_{i_{1}},\dots,X_{i_{k-1}}\big|\mathcal{E}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=2}^{m+1}I\big(X_{i_{k}};X_{i_{1}},\dots,X_{i_{k-1}}\big|\mathcal{E}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X;Y\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X;Y\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes conditional mutual information, and we use the convention that <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(X_{i_{1}};\emptyset\mid\mathcal{E})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(X_{i_{1}};\emptyset\mid\mathcal{E})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, conditional mutual information is bounded by marginal entropy:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\big(X_{i_{k}};X_{&lt;k}\mid\mathcal{E}\big)=H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H(X_{i_{k}}\mid X_{&lt;k},\mathcal{E})\leq H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\big(X_{i_{k}};X_{&lt;k}\mid\mathcal{E}\big)=H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})-H(X_{i_{k}}\mid X_{&lt;k},\mathcal{E})\leq H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{TC}\leq\sum_{k=2}^{m+1}H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>TC</mtext><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{TC}\leq\sum_{k=2}^{m+1}H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For any position <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with top-1 probability <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}^{*}=p_{k}(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}^{*}=p_{k}(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> and error rate <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k}=p(X_{i_{k}}\neq x_{i_{k}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq 1-p_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k}=p(X_{i_{k}}\neq x_{i_{k}}^{*}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq 1-p_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional entropy is bounded by:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq H_{b}(\epsilon_{k})+\epsilon_{k}\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(X_{i_{k}}\mid\mathcal{E})\leq H_{b}(\epsilon_{k})+\epsilon_{k}\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{b}(\epsilon)=-\epsilon\ln\epsilon-(1-\epsilon)\ln(1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{b}(\epsilon)=-\epsilon\ln\epsilon-(1-\epsilon)\ln(1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary entropy function, and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> is the vocabulary size.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The entropy is maximized when the remaining probability mass <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed uniformly over the <math id="A2.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|-1</annotation></semantics></math> non-optimal tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let the anchor have error rate <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{a}&lt;1-\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{a}&lt;1-\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and each of the <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> neighbors have error rate <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{n}&lt;1-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n}&lt;1-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex49.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">TC</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq H\big(X_{\text{anchor}}\mid\mathcal{E}\big)+\sum_{\text{neighbor }j}H\big(X_{j}\mid\mathcal{E}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>anchor</mtext></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mtext>neighbor </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq H\big(X_{\text{anchor}}\mid\mathcal{E}\big)+\sum_{\text{neighbor }j}H\big(X_{j}\mid\mathcal{E}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big[H_{b}(\epsilon_{a})+\epsilon_{a}\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]+m\cdot\Big[H_{b}(\epsilon_{n})+\epsilon_{n}\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big[H_{b}(\epsilon_{a})+\epsilon_{a}\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]+m\cdot\Big[H_{b}(\epsilon_{n})+\epsilon_{n}\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\Big[H_{b}(1-\kappa)+(1-\kappa)\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]+m\cdot\Big[H_{b}(1-\tau)+(1-\tau)\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\Big[H_{b}(1-\kappa)+(1-\kappa)\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big]+m\cdot\Big[H_{b}(1-\tau)+(1-\tau)\ln(|\mathcal{V}|-1)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Practical Relaxation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The conditions and bounds established above are <em id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">worst-case</em>, hence sufficient but not necessary.
In practice, several benign effects allow us to relax the certification condition and yield tighter realized bounds, without invalidating the theoretical guarantees.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding conditions and bounds are <em id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">worst-case</em>, i.e., sufficient but not necessary. In practice, several benign effects allow us to relax them without violating consistency. First, anchor confidence typically exceeds the trigger <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, and neighbor confidences often lie well above the acceptance floor <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, the realized error rates satisfy <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{a}\ll 1-\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{a}\ll 1-\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{n}\ll 1-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{n}\ll 1-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these realized rates into the cluster certificates (e.g., <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\kappa)+m(1-\tau)&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) tightens both the equivalence condition and the distributional bounds (<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and KL), yielding strictly smaller margins on the left-hand sides and thus strictly smaller risk budgets. Second, the effective neighborhood size at a decoding step is usually much smaller than the geometric radius would suggest: some positions within radius <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> may have been decoded already, and only a subset of masked positions will meet the acceptance rule in that step. Hence the operative <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathrm{effective}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>effective</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathrm{effective}}</annotation></semantics></math> is typically <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathrm{effective}}\ll 2W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>effective</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathrm{effective}}\ll 2W</annotation></semantics></math>, and one need not tune <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> by directly inverting the worst-case capacity <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\max}=\lfloor\kappa/(1-\tau)-1\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\max}=\lfloor\kappa/(1-\tau)-1\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, a slightly larger <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> can be safe because the certificates apply to <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathrm{effective}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>effective</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathrm{effective}}</annotation></semantics></math> rather than the geometric upper bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A second cluster of effects comes from local structure and iteration. Empirically, <em id="A2.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Local Determinism Propagation</em> implies nearby positions exhibit boosted reliability once an anchor is committed. This can be modeled as an effective confidence uplift <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{j}^{*}=p_{j}^{*}+\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{j}^{*}=p_{j}^{*}+\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for neighbors in the local window, equivalently <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}_{n}=\epsilon_{n}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}_{n}=\epsilon_{n}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, which again tightens the same certificates without changing their logical form. Moreover, clusters induced by different anchors often overlap; in the overlap region the redundant, mutually reinforcing evidence reduces the realized error further, effectively shrinking <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> in those cells. Finally, iterative refinement in dLLMs provides context amplification and self-correction: once some tokens are committed, they constrain subsequent predictions and can repair occasional sub-threshold decisions in later steps. Taken together, these effects explain why conservative, worst-case guarantees suffice for soundness, while practical deployments can safely adopt more permissive commitments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C Experiment Details ‣ Accelerating Diffusion LLM Inference via Local Determinism Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> provides the detailed configuration for each benchmark, including generation length and block length. The benchmarks include GSM8K (5-shot), MATH (4-shot), HumanEval (0-shot), MBPP (3-shot), and IFEval (0-shot).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A3.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configuration of Benchmarks</span>, including generation length and block length.</figcaption>
<div id="A3.T4.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:159.0pt;height:61.2pt;vertical-align:-28.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-15.6pt,6.0pt) scale(0.836098362615755,0.836098362615755) ;">
<table id="A3.T4.4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T4.4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Benchmark</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gen Len</span></td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.4.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Block Len</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">GSM8K</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">512</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">MATH</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.4.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">HumanEval</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.4.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">MBPP</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.4.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">IFEval</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">512</td>
<td id="A3.T4.4.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">32</td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Through the theoretical analysis in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ Accelerating Diffusion LLM Inference via Local Determinism Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, we derive strict equivalence conditions between LocalLeap and sequential greedy decoding, along with upper bounds on the number of decoded tokens per step. However, as mentioned in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS5" title="B.5 Practical Relaxation ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ Accelerating Diffusion LLM Inference via Local Determinism Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, practical applications often allow more relaxed conditions due to different distributional characteristics across models and datasets. In our experiments, we adopt slightly different hyperparameter settings for LLaDA-Instruct and Dream-Instruct, as shown in Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix C Experiment Details ‣ Accelerating Diffusion LLM Inference via Local Determinism Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="A3.T5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Configuration of hyperparameter</span>, including anchor trigger boundary <math id="A3.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, neighbor radius <math id="A3.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, and local relaxed boundary <math id="A3.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="A3.T5.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:159.0pt;height:33.1pt;vertical-align:-14.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-9.8pt,2.0pt) scale(0.890015242632905,0.890015242632905) ;">
